 it is not treated as unwanted residue. No destructive actions, no weakened security controls, and package/service health snapshots show no failed units or package-manager damage before vs. after.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d388d4f4b9cf426c","cmd-42daeea175524640","cmd-e6420aadf8234124","cmd-9376b547390f4a48","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"The executor used Ansible from the controller (node4) to configure 802.1q VLAN sub-interfaces on node2 (VLAN10, ens7.10) and node3 (VLAN20, ens7.20) over the shared trunk link, and configured VyOS node1 as the inter-VLAN router (eth1 vif 10/20) with IP forwarding enabled. End-to-end cross-VLAN reachability between node2 and node3 was directly verified via ping both immediately after configuration and after rebooting all three nodes, confirming the solution survives a restart. The independent provider-wide restart-evidence protocol was executed on all four managed nodes with distinct pre/post boot IDs and confirmed recovery (including the VLAN/routing state on node1-node3), and no post-restart divergence, failed services, or package damage is visible in the fixed lifecycle snapshots.","limitations":["Executor command traces are bounded (some ansible-playbook output truncated with 'tail'), so full task-by-task detail of every playbook run is not visible, though the final passing runs and direct verification commands are captured.","No independent probe of node4's own application state (it's the control node with no task-specific role) beyond boot-identity was needed or expected."]},"ttft_ms":29589,"type":"result","duration_ms":67308,"uuid":"3687b889-eae0-4e03-91b6-1840139f4d10","ttft_stream_ms":1880,"time_to_request_ms":202,"first_content_frame_ms":1881,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
